      "side": 1,
      "message": "Hi Siarhei Vishniakou, Thanks, auditing the logs makes a lot of sense. My only concern with disabling logs by default is: many app developers rely on monkey\u0027s stdout output to get crash/ANR info, so turning it off by default would break their workflows and log collection.\n\nFrom the freeze cases we\u0027ve seen so far, the culprit is specifically the blocking `System.err.println(s)` path (stdout). So instead of disabling logs by default, how about we add an option that only disables the stdout-type logging while keeping logcat on? That keeps default behavior (and developer-facing logs) intact, but lets stability/large-scale runs opt out of the blocking stdout writes.",
